    english_customer_response_template: 'Hi {{USERNAME}}, your computer was slow because the disk was working at full capacity almost all the time. We measured the real usage, identified the process that was saturating it, and applied the documented fix for that case. We also checked the physical health of the disk and it is in good condition, so no hardware replacement is needed. Your machine should now respond normally when opening programs and saving files. Please use it as usual for the rest of the day and reply to ticket {{TICKET_ID}} if you notice the slowness coming back, so we can check whether the same process is involved again.',
    english_technical_explanation: 'Sustained performance degradation on {{HOSTNAME}}. Get-Counter sampling showed % Disk Time above 90% with total processor time near saturation at {{TIMESTAMP}}. Top process analysis (Get-Process plus Process Explorer I/O columns) identified SysMain as the dominant disk consumer on a small HDD. Remediation: SysMain disabled and stopped as a documented test, after which % Disk Time dropped below 60% in normal use. Disk health verified with Get-PhysicalDisk (HealthStatus Healthy, no SSD failure). Startup reviewed and free space above 15%. Verification: user confirmed normal responsiveness; culprit process and action documented in ticket {{TICKET_ID}}.',
