    english_customer_response_template: 'Hi {{USERNAME}}, your computer was showing odd system errors and missing functions, which usually means some Windows internal files got damaged. We ran the standard repair sequence: first we restored the component store that Windows uses as its source of healthy files, and then we verified and repaired the system files themselves. Both processes completed successfully and the second full check came back clean. Your programs and personal files were not touched at any point. Please use the computer normally and confirm the errors are gone. If anything strange appears again, reply to ticket {{TICKET_ID}} with what you were doing at the time and we will take it from there.',
    english_technical_explanation: 'System instability on {{HOSTNAME}} after a failed update cycle. Repair followed the documented order: DISM /Online /Cleanup-Image /CheckHealth (corruption flagged), ScanHealth (deep scan, corruption confirmed), RestoreHealth completed 100% at {{TIMESTAMP}}, downloading healthy components from Windows Update. Afterward, sfc /scannow ran against the repaired store and reported "successfully repaired" with a clean second pass. CBS.log [SR] lines extracted as evidence; no unrecoverable member files remained. No alternative WIM source was required. Verification: CheckHealth and ScanHealth show no corruption, and the reported instability symptoms have not reproduced. No in-place upgrade needed.',
