    english_customer_response_template: 'Hi {{USERNAME}}, the application that was failing to start on your computer depends on a Windows service, and that service was not starting correctly. We read the system event log and found the exact reason: the account the service uses to run had an expired password. We updated the service configuration, set it to start automatically, and confirmed it is now running even after a full restart. The application should work normally now; please open it and try the task that was failing. If it stops again after a reboot, reply to ticket {{TICKET_ID}} and we will re-check the service events right away.',
    english_technical_explanation: 'Service startup failure on {{HOSTNAME}} at {{TIMESTAMP}}. sc qc showed the service binary path, start type, and SERVICE_START_NAME; System log events 7038 indicated the service could not log on with its configured account (expired password). Remediation: service credentials updated via sc config (obj= and password= syntax preserved), start type set to auto, and Start-Service brought it to Running. Dependencies verified with sc enumdepend to rule out a parent service failure. Verification: service Running after manual start and after a complete reboot, with no new 7000/7038 events in the System log. No gMSA or product reinstall required, so no L2 escalation.',
    keywords: ['servicio', 'service', 'services.msc', 'sc query', 'sc qc', '7000', '7038', '7031', '7011', 'dependencias', 'dependencies', 'cuenta de servicio', 'service account', 'start-service'],
