    english_customer_response_template: 'Hi {{USERNAME}}, your computer was taking several minutes to become usable after turning on. We measured the real boot time with the Windows performance log, reviewed everything that launches automatically at startup, and disabled the high-impact items that are not needed for your work. We also verified the disk is healthy and that fast startup is enabled. The next startup measured clearly faster, and the machine now reaches your desktop in well under a minute. Please keep an eye on it for a few days. If you install new software and startup slows down again, reply to ticket {{TICKET_ID}} and we will review the new startup entries.',
    english_technical_explanation: 'Slow boot on {{HOSTNAME}}: Diagnostics-Performance event 100 showed sustained boot times above 120 seconds at {{TIMESTAMP}}. Audit with Get-CimInstance Win32_StartupCommand, Task Manager startup impact, and Get-ScheduledTask identified multiple third-party updaters auto-launching at logon. Remediation: high-impact startup items disabled (not deleted), unnecessary third-party services unchecked via msconfig, and logon-triggered tasks disabled. Fast Startup verified active with powercfg /a; disk health and free space confirmed to rule out the 100% disk and full-disk brakes. Verification: next boot event 100 dropped below 60 seconds and the user confirmed a usable desktop earlier.',
