    english_customer_response_template: 'Hi {{USERNAME}}, your internet connection was working, but your computer could not translate website names into addresses, so pages and internal systems failed to open. We tested resolution against a public DNS to compare, found that the DNS servers assigned to your computer were not answering, cleared the local name cache, checked the hosts file for alterations, and restored the corporate DNS settings. Names now resolve correctly for both internal and external sites. Please test the sites and applications you normally use. If the problem returns after connecting to a VPN or another network, reply to ticket {{TICKET_ID}} and we will review the DNS assigned by that connection.',
