    english_customer_response_template: 'Hi {{USERNAME}}, your VPN was failing with error 809, which means the tunnel was being blocked before authentication, not that your password was wrong. We confirmed the VPN server was reachable, tested the tunnel ports from your network, and found that the network you were using blocks the ports this VPN needs. We validated the connection from a different network and it worked immediately, then re-tested from your location. Please use the VPN again and confirm you reach the internal systems. If you are in a hotel or shared network and it fails again, that network is likely blocking the tunnel; reply to ticket {{TICKET_ID}} and we will suggest the right protocol for that scenario.',
    english_technical_explanation: 'VPN failure for {{USERNAME}} from {{SOURCE_IP}} at {{TIMESTAMP}} with error 809. Classification: 800 unreachable, 809 tunnel filtering, 691 credentials, 812 NPS policy. Name resolution for vpn.{{DOMAIN}} succeeded; Test-NetConnection to port 443 passed, but UDP 500/4500 plus ESP required for L2TP were blocked on the source network. Account state verified (not locked, password valid), discarding 691; no NPS 6273 event involved, discarding 812. rasdial reproduced the error deterministically. Remediation: connection validated from an alternate network (mobile hotspot) successfully. Verification: VPN status Connected and internal resources reachable by name through the VPN DNS. If the error affected all users, remote-access infrastructure escalation would apply.',
    keywords: ['vpn', 'error 800', 'error 809', 'error 691', 'error 812', 'l2tp', 'sstp', 'ipsec', 'nps', '6273', 'rasdial', 'test-netconnection', 'acceso remoto'],
