    english_customer_response_template: 'Hi {{USERNAME}}, your network drive was showing a red cross and refusing to open. We tested the connection to the file server, which was healthy, and then found the real cause: your computer kept an old session against that server with previous credentials, which conflicts with the new mapping (this is the exact meaning of error 1219). We cleared the stale session and the saved old credentials, remapped the drive, and verified you can open it and create and read files with the permissions you were granted. Please restart your computer when convenient and confirm the drive still reconnects. If it fails again, reply to ticket {{TICKET_ID}}.',
