    escalation: 'Si el MTU debe ajustarse en la VPN/routers del sitio o el bloqueo viene de una regla global del firewall corporativo: escalar a redes — parámetro de infraestructura.',
    english_customer_response_template: 'Hi {{USERNAME}}, your internet connection responded to basic tests but web pages were loading halfway or not at all. We checked name resolution, proxy settings, and direct HTTPS connectivity, which were fine, and then tested your network for a size limitation on packets: your connection path cannot carry full-size packets, which breaks secure pages that transfer larger chunks of data. We lowered the network packet size setting on your computer to match the path, and pages now load completely. This situation is common after a VPN or a carrier change. Please test your regular sites and downloads. If partial loads return, reply to ticket {{TICKET_ID}}.',
    english_technical_explanation: 'Connectivity present but browsing broken on {{HOSTNAME}} at {{TIMESTAMP}}. DNS resolution verified (nslookup), proxy checked with netsh winhttp show proxy (clean), and transport to port 443 confirmed with Test-NetConnection, isolating a path-level issue. The fragmentation test ping with -f -l 1472 returned "Packet needs to be fragmented but DF set", proving the path MTU is lower than the interface default (typical after VPN or carrier change). Remediation: interface MTU set to 1400 with netsh interface ipv4 set subinterface store=persistent. Winsock reset was not required since the catalog was healthy, and no outbound firewall rules blocked the browser. Verification: internal and external pages load fully and network applications work.',
    keywords: ['ping ok no navega', 'winsock', 'netsh winsock reset', 'mtu', 'fragmentación', 'proxy', 'navegación', 'browser', 'test-netconnection', 'outbound', 'firewall', 'red', 'df set'],
