    escalation: 'Criterios de escalado a redes: paso 2 falla para varios equipos (switch/VLAN/AP), paso 3 falla para todo un sitio (routing/operadora), paso 4 falla en masa (DNS interno) — siempre con los outputs recogidos.',
    english_customer_response_template: 'Hi {{USERNAME}}, thank you for reporting the connectivity problem. We ran a complete layer-by-layer network check on your computer: local adapter and IP settings, local network reachability, internet path, and name resolution. Each test identified exactly which layer was failing, and we fixed the issue at that layer, so your connection is working again. We attached the full test output to ticket {{TICKET_ID}} for reference. If the problem happens again, the most useful detail you can give us is whether other people around you are affected at the same time, and whether it affects everything or only one application; that alone points us to the right layer immediately.',
    english_technical_explanation: 'Unspecified connectivity complaint from {{USERNAME}} on {{HOSTNAME}} at {{TIMESTAMP}}. Layered L1 workflow executed in order: ipconfig /all (valid IP, gateway, DNS, adapter state), ping to the gateway (local layer), ping to 8.8.8.8 (WAN/routing), nslookup (name resolution), tracert to locate the failing hop, and netstat -ano for application-specific connections. Results were mapped to the corresponding runbook and the ticket was classified by layer before resolution. Evidence attached: command outputs per step with timestamps. Verification: connectivity restored, or the case escalated to networks with the identified failing layer (for example site routing) instead of an unqualified "no network" statement.',
    keywords: ['workflow', 'metodología', 'escalera', 'network', 'ipconfig', 'ping', 'tracert', 'netstat', 'nslookup', 'diagnóstico', 'l1', 'l2', 'capas'],
