    english_customer_response_template: 'Hi {{USERNAME}}, Outlook was repeatedly asking for your password even though the password itself was correct. This usually happens because Windows keeps stored old credentials from before your last password change, and Outlook keeps trying them automatically. We removed those stored credentials, cleared the Office identity cache so the app authenticates from scratch, and confirmed your client supports modern authentication. Outlook is now open and syncing your mail normally; please let it run during the day and confirm you do not get the password prompt again. If it ever reappears after a password change, reply to ticket {{TICKET_ID}} and we will clear the stored credentials again.',
    english_technical_explanation: 'Outlook password prompt loop for {{USERNAME}} on {{HOSTNAME}} at {{TIMESTAMP}}. Credentials verified valid in portal.office.com, discarding account lockout or MFA registration issues. Root cause: stale saved credentials in Windows Credential Manager (MSOffice16 / MicrosoftOffice16_Data entries against login.microsoftonline.com and outlook.office365.com) left over from a recent password change. Remediation: entries removed via the stored credentials dialog (rundll32.exe keymgr.dll,KRShowKeyMgr) and the Office identity cache cleared by deleting HKCU Identities, forcing a fresh Modern Auth (OAuth) token. Add-in interference ruled out with outlook.exe /safe. Verification: Outlook syncs without prompting for a full working day with automatic send/receive active.',
    keywords: ['outlook', 'contraseña', 'password prompt', 'bucle', 'loop', 'credential manager', 'keymgr', 'modern auth', 'oauth', 'identities', 'm365', 'app password', 'basic auth'],
