    english_customer_response_template: 'Hi {{USERNAME}}, OneDrive was failing with error 0x8004de40, which is an authentication problem between your computer and the cloud service, not a password issue. The most common cause is a small clock drift on the computer, which breaks the secure certificate validation; your clock was indeed a few minutes off. We synchronized it with the company time source, reset the sync client, and relinked your account. The sync icon is green again and your files are uploading normally. Please check OneDrive during the day; if the same error code appears again, reply to ticket {{TICKET_ID}} and we will apply the deeper repair steps we have documented for persistent cases.',
    english_technical_explanation: 'OneDrive failing with 0x8004de40 on {{HOSTNAME}} at {{TIMESTAMP}}. Web access to SharePoint and OneDrive worked, discarding a service outage and isolating the client. Root cause: system clock drift breaking TLS certificate validation (first documented cause for this error code). Remediation: time resynchronized with w32tm /resync; client reset via onedrive.exe /reset; account unlinked and relinked to rebuild authentication. TLS 1.2 registry values were verified healthy (Windows 10/11 defaults). The documented DLL re-registration (oleaut32, actxprxy, msxml3) was not required after the clock fix. Verification: sync icon green, library syncing, and no recurrence of 0x8004de40 within 24 hours of use. Single machine affected, so no TLS-inspection escalation.',
    keywords: ['0x8004de40', 'onedrive', 'sharepoint', 'sync', 'tls 1.2', 'w32tm', 'resync', 'regsvr32', 'oleaut32', 're-autenticación', 'm365', 'error', 'reloj', 'clock'],
